Mission Local reported that MEDA was purchasing the four-story building at 2901 16th St., two blocks east of the 16th Street BART station, to rehabilitate it into 62 units of permanent affordable housing. The project was contingent on city approval of a loan for the purchase. The units were planned for the building’s upper three floors, with the ground-floor businesses remaining below.

